<< /A << /O /Layout /Placement /Block >> /Alt (Forest plot showing the mean differences between experimental and control groups across four studies. Each study's mean, standard deviation, total, and weight are listed, with all studies favoring the experimental group. The overall effect shows a mean difference of 2.58 with a 95% confidence interval of 1.27 to 3.90. The test for overall effect is significant with a p-value of 0.0001. The plot includes individual study estimates as squares and the combined estimate as a diamond.) /K 465 0 R /P 230 0 R /Pg 226 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
